WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
In nineteen-oh-one, no woman in
Britain could vote in a general

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.910
election.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.410
Some campaigners used peaceful
meetings and petitions.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.470
Others used direct action,
and some broke the law.

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.910
How much did the law-breakers help?

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.130
Historians still debate it.

7
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.010
Meanwhile, in the nineteen
twenties and thirties,

8
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.450
several countries moved away from
democracy, towards dictators.

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.890
Why would people support leaders
who crushed their freedom?

10
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.830
In this mission, you'll compare
suffragists and suffragettes,

11
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.810
find two key years for women's
votes, and meet three dictators.

12
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.410
Your mission: explain why
democracy grew in Britain,

13
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.940
but not everywhere.
